You are auditing my website for production-readiness. Check the site at [URL / repo path] against the 20-item checklist below. Inspect the actual code and live pages; don't assume anything exists.

For each item, report:
- Status: PASS / FAIL / PARTIAL
- Evidence: file path, URL, or snippet showing what you found
- Fix: if not PASS, apply the fix (or list exact changes if you can't)

CHECKLIST
1. Custom 404 page: a branded 404 with navigation back home, returning a real 404 status code.
2. Meta title on every page: unique, under ~60 characters.
3. Meta description on every page: unique, ~150-160 characters.
4. CTA above the fold: a clear primary call to action visible without scrolling on desktop and mobile.
5. Complete favicon set: .ico, 16x16, 32x32, apple-touch-icon (180x180), Android icons (192/512), and site.webmanifest.
6. robots.txt: exists at the root, doesn't accidentally block important pages, and references the sitemap.
7. sitemap.xml: exists, lists all public pages with valid URLs, and is submitted or referenced in robots.txt.
8. Open Graph image: og:title, og:description, og:image (1200x630), og:url, plus Twitter card tags on every page.
9. Alt text on every image: descriptive; empty alt only for decorative images.
10. Mobile breakpoints: layout works at 320, 375, 768, 1024, and 1440px with no horizontal scroll or overlapping elements; viewport meta tag is present.
11. Sticky mobile CTA: a persistent call/WhatsApp/contact button on mobile that doesn't cover content.
12. Loading states: spinners or skeletons for async content and form submissions; buttons are disabled while submitting.
13. Form error states: inline validation, clear error messages, a success state, and server-side validation.
14. Thank-you page: shown after form submission, ideally with its own URL for conversion tracking.
15. Privacy policy page: exists, is linked in the footer, and matches the data actually collected.
16. Terms & Conditions page: exists and is linked in the footer.
17. Cookie banner: shown if cookies or tracking are used; lets users accept or reject, and doesn't load non-essential trackers before consent.
18. Analytics setup: GA4/Plausible/etc. installed, firing correctly, with conversion events (form submit, CTA click, calls).
19. Real contact information: no placeholder text, fake phone numbers, example.com emails, or "Lorem ipsum"; links like tel: and mailto: work.
20. Compressed images: modern formats (WebP/AVIF), sensible dimensions, lazy loading below the fold, and no image over ~200KB without reason.

ALSO CHECK (bonus)
- HTTPS and redirects (http→https, www→non-www or the reverse)
- Canonical tags
- Lighthouse scores (Performance, Accessibility, SEO, Best Practices)
- Console errors, broken links, and leftover TODO/placeholder content

OUTPUT FORMAT
1. A summary table: # | Item | Status | Notes
2. A prioritized list of fixes (critical → nice-to-have)
3. Apply all fixes you can safely make, then re-verify and show a final table.

Don't skip items. If you can't verify something, mark it UNVERIFIED and say why.